<title>UK: TransTec buys Vector, plans share placing.</title>
<headline>TransTec buys Vector, plans share placing.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK engineering group TransTec Plc said on Monday it was buying Vector Plastics for 18.1 million stg and planned to raise nine million stg through a share placing to fund the purchase.  </p>
<p>TransTec expects that as a result of the acquisition, operating profits will not be less than 1.2 million stg in the full year.</p>
<p>It said the purchase would enhance pre-exceptional earnings this year and would also be earnings enhancing in 1998.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
